***conformance tests***

# all-concepts-visible
The parsed `valid.plain` of read-scenarios has no concept error with the visible concepts Task, TaskList, App and User.

# missing-concept
With the visible concepts Task, App and User, it gives exactly the three errors `Syntax error at line 10 in test plain file 'valid.plain': Concept ⟨TaskList⟩ used in scenario `add-first-task` is not defined in module 'task-manager'.`, and the same for line 14 and `add-without-name`, and line 26 and `gherkin-shape`.

# predefined-concepts
A parsed file whose scenario `works` on line 8 has the text `⟨ConformanceTests⟩ start ⟨Implementation⟩.` has no concept error with no visible concept.

***acceptance tests***
